> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Why SQLite ALONE can't be the only database:**
> SQLite is a **local, single-file database** that lives on the device. It does NOT support:
> - Multiple users accessing the same data simultaneously
> - Real-time sync across Website + Android + iOS
> - Server-side geospatial queries (finding shops within X km)
> - Concurrent write operations from thousands of users
>
> **Our Solution:** Use SQLite on each device as a **local cache** for offline mode and fast reads, but keep **PostgreSQL on the server** as the single source of truth. All 3 platforms connect to the SAME PostgreSQL server via APIs, ensuring real-time sync.

